//! The `break-inside` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets how
//! page, column, or region breaks should behave inside a generated box. If there is no generated
//! box, the property is ignored.
//!
//! Initial: auto. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - auto: Allows, but does not force, any break (page, column, or region) to be inserted within the
//! principal box.
//! - avoid: Avoids any break (page, column, or region) from being inserted within the principal box.
//! - avoid-column: Avoids any column break within the principal box.
//! - avoid-page: Avoids any page break within the principal box.
//! - avoid-region: Avoids any region break within the principal box.
//!
//! Grammar: auto | avoid | avoid-page | avoid-column | avoid-region
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-break-4/#propdef-break-inside
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/break-inside
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

